     If ``newstyle`` is activated, the callables are wrapped to work like
     newstyle callables.  See :ref:`newstyle-gettext` for more information.
 
+    ``cache_size`` controls an optional bounded LRU cache of raw
+    translation results.  ``0`` (the default) disables caching and
+    calls the provider every time.  A positive integer caches results
+    of ``gettext``, ``ngettext``, ``pgettext``, and ``npgettext`` up to
+    that many entries per function, evicting least-recently-used entries.
+
+    ``cache_partition`` is an arbitrary hashable value that distinguishes
+    translation state.  Applications whose translations depend on locale
+    or request state should set this to a value unique to each state.
+    When the partition is changed with
+    :meth:`set_translation_cache_partition`, the cache is cleared.
+
+    Caching wraps the raw provider callables before new-style wrapping
+    and formatting, so formatting variables are not part of cache keys.
+
+    .. versionchanged:: 3.2
+        Added ``cache_size`` and ``cache_partition``.
+
     .. versionchanged:: 3.0
         Added ``pgettext`` and ``npgettext``.
 
     .. versionadded:: 2.5
         Added new-style gettext support.
 
+.. method:: jinja2.Environment.set_translation_cache_partition(value)
+
+    Set the current cache partition and clear all cached translation
+    results.  The partition is used as part of the cache key so that
+    different partitions (e.g. locales, request states) do not share
+    cached entries.
+
+    .. versionadded:: 3.2
+
+.. method:: jinja2.Environment.clear_translation_cache()
+
+    Clear all cached translation results.  Has no effect if caching
+    is disabled.
+
+    .. versionadded:: 3.2
+
+.. method:: jinja2.Environment.resize_translation_cache(capacity)
+
+    Resize the translation cache to ``capacity``.  A capacity of ``0``
+    disables and clears the cache.  Negative capacities raise
+    :exc:`ValueError`.
+
+    .. versionadded:: 3.2
+
